# Design: storage of the source workspace

## Problem

Antigravity records carry no working directory. The hub needs a place
for the workspace that the device reports, and a rule that gives each
session a cwd without a re-derivation of the hub.

## Approach

- The value belongs to the source (`sources.workspace_path`), not to
  the session. One source is one Antigravity conversation, and one
  value per source is enough for every session of that source.
- `SetSourceWorkspace` fills the sessions that have no cwd and stores
  the column in one transaction. The fill comes first. A crash between
  the two statements leaves no half state.
- The fill also copies the repository of a known `workspaces` row of the
  same device, so a session that already has an observation gets its
  repository in the same write.
- Ingest reads the column in its source query. `applySessionDelta` uses
  the workspace only when the session has no cwd and the records of the
  batch carry none. The rule is the same in `finalizeSession` of a
  re-derivation.
- The tombstone carries the column. Without it, a reallow would create
  a source row without a workspace, and write-once would need an
  exception for that one case.
- `workspacePathProblem` holds the path checks of a workspace
  observation. The source workspace uses the same checks, so the two
  writes cannot drift apart. The error text of an observation is
  unchanged.
- `SourcesWithoutWorkspace` lists the sources of one device and agent
  that have no workspace. It runs on the writer, like the other source
  reads of a pass.

## Key Trade-offs

- The first path is final. Antigravity keeps one workspace per
  conversation, and a second value would need a rule for the sessions
  that already have the first one.
- Schema 9 forces one full recovery copy of the hub database at the
  next `ohya setup` after the upgrade.

## Gotchas

- `migrate_released_test.go` needs no edit. Its released list stops at
  schema 8, so it exercises the 8 to 9 upgrade.
- `sources.file_identity` is declared and documented, but no code
  writes it. It is recorded in NOTES.md for a later schema change.
